comments.body:
The `prevCountRef` is only updated in the non-increase path. When `notificationCount` increases, the effect returns early and leaves `prevCountRef.current` stale, which can incorrectly trigger the shake on later decreases (e.g., 5→4 still compares against 3). Update `prevCountRef.current` on every change (including the increase path) before returning/cleaning up the timer.
```suggestion
    const prevCount = prevCountRef.current;
    prevCountRef.current = notificationCount;

    // Trigger shake animation when notification count increases
    if (notificationCount > prevCount) {
      setIsShaking(true);
      const timer = setTimeout(() => setIsShaking(false), 500);
      return () => clearTimeout(timer);
    }
```
